shape theory.emergence.non-commutativity : theory.emergence.general-composition {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 6.5 (Non-Commutativity).
// Composition is generally non-commutative: A compose_S B is not
// structurally equivalent to B compose_S A when S distinguishes
// its operands by role.
//
// If S assigns different structural roles to its operands (as any
// asymmetric coupling does), swapping A and B changes which shape
// occupies which role. Different role assignments produce different
// contact geometry, hence different emergent character.
//
// Commutativity holds in special cases: when A and B have identical
// structure, or when S is symmetric with respect to its operands.
//
// The transformation law M' = f(C, S) has inherent directionality:
// C is input, M' is output. Asymmetry is the default; symmetry
// requires justification.
//
// Derives from: theory.emergence.general-composition
  """
}
